# Text files are stored with LF and checked out with LF on every platform,
# whatever core.autocrlf says: the bash scripts (scripts/*.sh) and
# scripts/pbs.lock break with CRLF, which a Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true (the default on GitHub's Windows runners) would
# otherwise produce. Files git detects as binary are left untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf
